{"answer":null,"company_tags":[],"concept_id":"cuda-ld-cache-hint-modifiers","content_sha256":"sha256:8476a47340efe494a2e451f6b8046889171f7982b847523df71ca9b682d463dc","correct_option_ids":["a"],"created_at":1789956503.511882,"domain":"operator-development","explanation":".ca 在 L1+L2 正常缓存(适合会复用的数据);.cg 绕过 L1 只在 L2 缓存;.cs(streaming)按最低复用优先级缓存,专为只读一次的流式数据设计,减少对将被复用数据的缓存污染。因此一次性大流式读用 .cs/__ldcs 最合适。","id":"q-op-mag3-cuda-ld-cache-hint-modifiers-001","options":[{"id":"a","text":".cs(streaming),它以流式/最低驻留优先级经过缓存,尽量不污染 L1/L2、避免把还会复用的数据挤出缓存"},{"id":"b","text":".ca,因为它会把数据长期钉在 L1 里"},{"id":"c","text":".cg 一定比 .cs 更省带宽"},{"id":"d","text":"三者对缓存行为完全一致,只是语法不同"}],"prompt":"PTX 的 load 缓存修饰符 .ca、.cg、.cs(对应 __ldca/__ldcg/__ldcs)含义不同。对读一次、之后不再复用的大流式数组,最合适的是?","review_state":null,"schema_version":"question/v1","skill":"optimization","source_refs":[{"kind":"official_docs","title":"PTX ISA","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/parallel-thread-execution/index.html"},{"kind":"official_docs","title":"CUDA C++ Programming Guide","url":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/index.html"}],"status":"enabled","topic":"cuda","type":"single_choice","wiki_refs":[]}
